<p>

The Conference PhysCon2013 will focus on the borderland between Physics and Control with 
emphasis on both theory and applications. Topics will include many topics among them,
Nonlinear dynamics, 
Mathematics,  
Dynamics and control of complex networks, 
Self-organization and complexity, 
Engineering methods and applied fields ...  See the web-site of
<a href="http://www.ipicyt.edu.mx/physcon2013/">  PhysCon-2013 </a><br> 
<p></p>
The invited session CCSNSO'13 relies precisely on the topics listed above, in order
to study the control of complex systems and complex networks. 
The meeting is concerned with multidisciplinary approaches aimed at exploring, visualizing, 
modeling and simulating large scale dynamic networks, 
in order to detect and control their emergent communities, to analyse self-organizing processes, such as synchronization 
and to characterize their evolution.

<p></p>

A FINIR .... .... .... .... ... :   

Complex systems are composed of interacting entities. These entities are supported by structural organization 
like networks and emergent properties appear in relation with these supports. The structural organization and 
its topology can also be the result of the emergent properties. In both cases, self-organizations of entities 
and their structural or emergent support is one of the main issue of the complexity of these systems. 
Our workshop/symposium deals with modeling these phenomena and to understand how controling these complex systems 
preserving their native complexity and so the emergent self-organization. The expected submissions can cover
 two approaches : the first one is an adaptation of the control theory for complex dynamical systems and the second 
 ones concerns heuristics dealing with modeling control over behavioral systems. Two examples of such problems
  could be the synchronization of complex networks and the modeling of crowd behavior ...   

JE CORRIGE  DEMAIN ...

